  "transcript": [
    {
      "s": 0.0,
      "e": 1.76,
      "text": "Apollo 12"
    },
    {
      "s": 1.76,
      "e": 3.42,
      "text": "Pete Conrad, Commander"
    },
    {
      "s": 3.42,
      "e": 4.8,
      "text": "Richard Gordon, Command Module Pilot"
    },
    {
      "s": 4.8,
      "e": 5.94,
      "text": "Alan Bean, Lunar Module Pilot"
    },
    {
      "s": 5.94,
      "e": 7.94,
      "text": "Ignition sequence start in"
    },
    {
      "s": 7.94,
      "e": 8.68,
      "text": "Six"
    },
    {
      "s": 8.68,
      "e": 9.36,
      "text": "Five"
    },
    {
      "s": 9.36,
      "e": 10.4,
      "text": "Four"
    },
    {
      "s": 10.4,
      "e": 11.24,
      "text": "Three"
    },
    {
      "s": 11.24,
      "e": 12.14,
      "text": "Two"
    },
    {
      "s": 12.14,
      "e": 13.04,
      "text": "One"
    },
    {
      "s": 13.04,
      "e": 13.98,
      "text": "Zero"
    },
    {
      "s": 13.98,
      "e": 14.96,
      "text": "All engines running"
    },
    {
      "s": 14.96,
      "e": 16.96,
      "text": "Commit lift-off"
    },
    {
      "s": 16.96,
      "e": 21.28,
      "text": "Pete Conrad reports the yaw program is in."
    },
    {
      "s": 23.32,
      "e": 25.48,
      "text": "Tower clear"
    },
    {
      "s": 26.24,
      "e": 30.44,
      "text": "Apollo 12 was struck by lightning seconds after launch twice."
    },
    {
      "s": 30.44,
      "e": 31.36,
      "text": "I don't know what happened here."
    },
    {
      "s": 31.36,
      "e": 33.56,
      "text": "We had everything in the world drop out."
    },
    {
      "s": 33.56,
      "e": 37.24,
      "text": "I got three fuel cell lights, an AC bus light, a fuel cell disconnect"
    },
    {
      "s": 37.24,
      "e": 41.0,
      "text": "AC bus overload 1 and 2, main bus A and B out"
    },
    {
      "s": 41.0,
      "e": 46.8,
      "text": "Luckily, Flight controller John Aaron had seen the same unusual readings in a flight simulation."
    },
    {
      "s": 46.8,
      "e": 48.96,
      "text": "The fix was resetting an obscure system called Signal Conditioning Equipment (SCE)."
    },
    {
      "s": 48.96,
      "e": 52.68,
      "text": "Apollo 12, Houston, try SCE to Auxiliary, over"
    },
    {
      "s": 52.68,
      "e": 55.0,
      "text": "NCE to Auxiliary?"
    },
    {
      "s": 55.0,
      "e": 56.12,
      "text": "What the hell's that?"
    },
    {
      "s": 56.12,
      "e": 59.52,
      "text": "S-C-E, S-C-E to Auxiliary"
    },
    {
      "s": 59.84,
      "e": 63.36,
      "text": "Apollo 12, Houston,  try to reset your fuel cells now"
    },
    {
      "s": 63.44,
      "e": 70.52,
      "text": "Okay. I have a good GDC, and Al has got the fuel cells back on, and we'll be working on our AC buses."
    },
    {
      "s": 70.52,
      "e": 78.8,
      "text": "Automatic guidance brought Apollo 12 to their target on the Ocean of Storms."
    },
    {
      "s": 78.8,
      "e": 81.24,
      "text": "Conrad and Bean made a precision landing just 535 feet from the Surveyor 3 spacecraft."
    },
    {
      "s": 81.24,
      "e": 84.32,
      "text": "There it is! Son of a gun- straight down the middle of the road! I can't believe it!"
    },
    {
      "s": 84.32,
      "e": 86.68,
      "text": "Amazing! Fantastic!"
    },
    {
      "s": 86.72,
      "e": 91.16,
      "text": "Man, that may have been a small one for Neil, but that's a long one for me"
    },
    {
      "s": 95.9,
      "e": 98.86,
      "text": "Pete Conrad &  Alan Bean did two moonwalks in two days"
    },
    {
      "s": 98.86,
      "e": 101.18,
      "text": "They collected lunar samples ..."
    },
    {
      "s": 101.18,
      "e": 105.26,
      "text": "retrieved parts of Surveyor 3 to study the long-term effects of exposure ..."
    },
    {
      "s": 105.26,
      "e": 111.68,
      "text": "and deployed the first Apollo Lunar Surface Experiments Package (ALSEP) to study ..."
    },
    {
      "s": 111.68,
      "e": 113.92,
      "text": "moonquakes"
    },
    {
      "s": 113.92,
      "e": 116.38,
      "text": "ions"
    },
    {
      "s": 116.38,
      "e": 118.56,
      "text": "magnetic fields"
    },
    {
      "s": 118.56,
      "e": 120.26,
      "text": "solar wind"
    },
    {
      "s": 120.28,
      "e": 122.32,
      "text": "and lunar dust"
    },
    {
      "s": 127.42,
      "e": 131.42,
      "text": "The ascent module was jettisoned to impact the moon."
    },
    {
      "s": 131.42,
      "e": 136.48,
      "text": "countdown LM impact in 3 2 1 ... mark"
    },
    {
      "s": 136.48,
      "e": 140.08,
      "text": "NASA observed seismic activity on the Moon for the first time."
    },
    {
      "s": 140.08,
      "e": 143.88,
      "text": "To the surprise of seismologists, some signals lasted an hour."
    },
    {
      "s": 144.02,
      "e": 146.9,
      "text": "Hello Houston, Apollo 12 en route home"
    },
    {
      "s": 148.36,
      "e": 151.48,
      "text": "We're getting a spectacular view of the eclipse."
    },
    {
      "s": 153.56,
      "e": 157.94,
      "text": "Splashdown November 24, 1969"
    },
    {
      "s": 162.1,
      "e": 167.08,
      "text": "Designed for a life of one year, ALSEP continued to send data back for 8 years."
    },
    {
      "s": 170.42,
      "e": 175.0,
      "text": "The lunar samples are still studied today."
    }
  ],
